{"t": 1794119141.2698224, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found & fixed*\n\nCause: `reports/export.py` used a csv.DictWriter with fixed `fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\"]`. Ledger 2026.11 added a `currency` key to every row, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` (~4,120 failures in CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api`, eu-west-1).\n\nFix: set `extrasaction=\"ignore\"` on the writer so unknown upstream fields no longer crash the export and the existing `id,amount` CSV contract is preserved. Verified with rows containing `currency`.\n\nNote: `currency` is not emitted in the CSV \u2014 flag if Finance needs it added as a column. Needs a redeploy of reports-api to take effect."}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794119149.3149734, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_get_channel_history", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "limit": 10}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794119157.9992592, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502: fixed in reports/export.py (csv DictWriter now ignores extra upstream fields; ledger 2026.11 added `currency`). Redeploy needed."}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794119159.4270759, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_get_channel_history", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "limit": 20}, "ok": true}
